<!--
    ELF GOT data imports (`option importdata on|off`, pass `elfgotimports`).

    Issue: a -fPIC read of data another image defines loads a GOT slot the
    dynamic loader fills with the symbol's address (R_*_GLOB_DAT), then loads
    through it. kuna painted PE and Mach-O import slots externref but never an
    ELF GOT slot, so the read printed as `*dat_<slot>` (libcurl, libssl and
    libxml2 on this host all read stdout, environ or a library global that way).

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding, the ELF GOT import slots
    (`kuna-analysis/src/loader/kuna_elfgotimports.rs`: reported as import slots,
    named and painted externref), rendered by P9 naming-policy
    `PrintC::op_load` (`importdata`).

    P0 assertion: `option importdata on|off` (default off). The ELF slot facts
    are committed under the same gate, so it is set after `load file` and before
    the `read symbols` that commits them.

    Fixtures: `elf_gotdata_x86_64.so` and `elf_gotdata_aarch64.so` (built from
    `elf_gotdata.c`, see the fixtures README). `get_counter` reads the undefined
    `imported_counter`; `get_exported` reads `exported_value`, a symbol the object
    defines, whose GLOB_DAT slot `dynrelocs` already folds.

    Pass 1 / 3 (the default, the BUG): `get_counter` returns `*dat_2680` /
    `*dat_205c0`. Pass 2 / 4 (`option importdata on`, the FIX): it returns
    `imported_counter`. `get_exported` returns `exported_value` in all four
    passes: a defined symbol's slot is never painted.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
